    "control": "controls/yaml/catalog.yaml",
    "scope": "One YAML document from local bytes passed to YAML::Load(std::string): block and flow collections, quoted and block scalars, anchors and aliases, as a typed tree in source order. Plain scalars are typed by the adapter with YAML 1.2 core-schema patterns and converted by yaml-cpp's Node::as<T>; yaml-cpp itself resolves plain nulls and keeps '?' (plain) versus '!' (non-plain) tags.",
    "family": "yaml-cpp own scanner and SingleDocParser",
    "family_note": "Own scanner (src/scanner.cpp, scantoken.cpp, scanscalar.cpp) and SingleDocParser building a node graph through NodeBuilder; no delegation to libyaml or another YAML parser.",
    "typing_note": "yaml-cpp has no YAML 1.2 core-schema resolver: its convert<bool> also accepts YAML 1.1 words (y, yes, on). The adapter applies the 1.2 core patterns only to '?' scalars, so quoted strings stay strings. The controls contain no scalar whose type differs between the schemas.",
