    "name": "rapidyaml",
    "version": "0.16.0",
    "license": "MIT",
    "license_evidence": "https://github.com/biojppm/rapidyaml/blob/v0.16.0/LICENSE.txt (MIT); the bundled c4core sources in the release archive are MIT as well.",
    "input_api": "ryml::parse_in_arena(ryml::csubstr) into a ryml::Tree, then Tree::resolve() for aliases; Tree::is_map/is_seq/key/val/is_val_quoted/val_is_null/has_val_tag traversal and c4::atoi/c4::atod",
    "documentation": "https://github.com/biojppm/rapidyaml/blob/v0.16.0/src/c4/yml/parse.hpp",
    "documentation_evidence": "parse.hpp documents the parse_in_arena overloads that copy the YAML source into the tree arena and parse it into the root node; samples/quickstart.cpp at the same tag documents Tree::resolve() for anchors and aliases and the val_is_null/is_val_quoted style queries.",
    "source": "https://github.com/biojppm/rapidyaml/releases/tag/v0.16.0",
    "source_sha256": "a0ce80a8f4211580c8703e57acb813a28ca6ec80908f6eb926be94be8e98d39d",
    "adapter": "projects/yaml/cpp/rapidyaml/harness.cpp",
    "control": "controls/yaml/catalog.yaml",
    "scope": "One YAML document from local bytes passed to ryml::parse_in_arena, with aliases expanded by Tree::resolve(): block and flow collections, quoted and block scalars, anchors and aliases, as a typed tree in source order. Unquoted non-null scalars are typed by the adapter with YAML 1.2 core-schema patterns and converted with c4core atoi/atod; rapidyaml itself reports scalar style and plain nulls.",
    "family": "rapidyaml (ryml) own ParseEngine over c4core",
    "family_note": "Own event-driven ParseEngine (src/c4/yml/parse_engine.def.hpp) with a tree event handler, built from the release source archive with its bundled c4core; no delegation to libyaml or another YAML parser. The Python rapidyaml binding is the same family.",
    "typing_note": "rapidyaml keeps scalars as text with style bits and has no core-schema typing of its own. The adapter applies the YAML 1.2 core patterns only to unquoted, non-null scalars, so quoted and block scalars stay strings. The controls contain no scalar whose type differs between the schemas.",
    "build_note": "Built with RYML_DEFAULT_CALLBACK_USES_EXCEPTIONS so the documented default error callback throws instead of aborting.",
